  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "509fc449-f9bf-4021-bfdc-3c272650bb1a",
      "question": "As of the March 5, 2026 market close, how likely are NVIDIA (NVDA), Apple (AAPL), Microsoft (MSFT), Tesla (TSLA) and JPMorgan Chase (JPM) to post a positive five-session return, and how likely is each to fall more than 5%?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T18:57:28.997122Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T18:58:24.276071Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "As of **March 5, 2026 market close (21:00 UTC)**, Kumo Relational estimated the following probabilities. Both predictions use that anchor. [1][2]\n\n| Stock | Probability of positive return | Probability of return below −5% | Evidence |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| NVIDIA (NVDA) | 61.9% | 28.5% | [1][2] |\n| Apple (AAPL) | 58.9% | 18.0% | [1][2] |\n| Microsoft (MSFT) | 61.0% | 16.8% | [1][2] |\n| Tesla (TSLA) | 60.8% | 17.9% | [1][2] |\n| JPMorgan Chase (JPM) | 62.1% | 12.6% | [1][2] |\n\n**Horizon caveat:** The templates target five-session adjusted-close returns, but count qualifying outcomes within **five calendar days after the anchor**. These estimates therefore should not be treated as an unrestricted forecast for the next five trading sessions. [1][2]\n\nThese are model probabilities, not observed returns or guarantees.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] NVIDIA Kumo prediction result — positive_return — evidence `hermes-receipt:d70156ccdf8407dd303a96bc4eb3dbd02225865060c76e146107d2b615caf32e`\n- [2] NVIDIA Kumo prediction result — material_downside — evidence `hermes-receipt:4690e1b744254d8c1664d5033a5811458c1ba4cfd8e77e9c4e7faa0d550c6fac`",
